ercent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\r\n\r\n- Reproducible in 4.4-dev4\r\n\r\n### System information\r\n\r\nGodot v4.4.dev4 - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue Oct  8 03:11:08 UTC 2024 on X11 - X11 display driver, Single-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Laptop GPU - AMD Ryzen 9 5900HX with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)\r\n\r\n### Issue description\r\n\r\nIn the `Monitors` of the debugger there are many values that apparently are floats and which with [this pull](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/47502) now turned a bit ugly/unnecessary:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a93043b9-1b23-4a9c-bf6b-21734e702477)\r\n\r\nI don't expect that the number of nodes or draw calls could be anything other than an integer? *Many* items in the Monitor list should either be an integer or not display the decimal. Besides the values, the same goes for the little graphs containing floats (Nodes: 31.0, **23.25**, **15.5**, **7.75**).\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nOpen up *any* project and go to Monitors to have a look at the values & graphs.\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\r\n\r\nNot relevant.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.githu